.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt NOD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nod
.Nd suckless notification daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a minimal notification daemon for X11 that implements enough of the
Desktop Notifications Specification 1.2 over D-Bus to work with
.Xr notify-send 1
and any application that emits standard notifications.
.Pp
.Nm
claims the well-known name
.Pa org.freedesktop.Notifications
on the session bus and displays notifications as cards in a single
override-redirect X11 window, laid out and painted by the CUI library
through its SDL3 renderer.
Only one notification daemon can own that name at a time.
.Pp
Configuration is compile-time only: edit
.Pa config.h
and rebuild.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Print version and exit.
.El
.Sh INTERACTION
.Bl -tag -width "Action button "
.It Sy Stack
Several notifications fold into a deck, newest in front;
hovering unfolds it into a list.
.It Sy Action button
One button per action (up to three); clicking it emits
.Sy ActionInvoked
with that key, then dismisses.
With
.Sy action_buttons
off, a left click on the card invokes the
.Dq default
action (or the first one).
.It Sy Dismiss
Dismiss without invoking any action.
Right-clicking a card, or swiping it towards the screen edge
(mouse drag or two-finger touchpad swipe), does the same.
.It Sy Hover
Timeouts are held while the pointer is over the stack.
.It Sy Timeout
Auto-dismiss after the notification's expire time.
.El
.Sh SUPPORTED HINTS
.Bl -tag -width "urgency (byte)  "
.It Sy urgency No (byte)
0 = low, 1 = normal, 2 = critical.
Selects colors and default timeout from
.Pa config.h .
.El
.Pp
All other hints are ignored.
HTML/pango markup in
.Sy summary
and
.Sy body
is stripped; only plain text is rendered.
.Sh CAPABILITIES
.Nm
advertises
.Sy body
and
.Sy actions
via
.Sy GetCapabilities .
It does not advertise
.Sy body-markup ,
.Sy body-images ,
.Sy icon-static ,
.Sy persistence ,
or
.Sy sound .
.Sh SIGNALS
.Bl -tag -width "SIGUSR1 "
.It Sy SIGINT , SIGTERM
Clean up windows, release the D-Bus name, exit.
.It Sy SIGUSR1
Reload colors and font from X resources.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "config.def.h "
.It Pa config.h
Per-user appearance, card parts (app name, urgency, time, dividers,
buttons, border), stacking, motion, timeouts and position.
Copied from
.Pa config.def.h
on first build.
.El
.Sh COMPOSITING
With a compositor running,
.Nm
uses a 32-bit window with real transparency and antialiased corners;
without one it shapes the window with the X Shape extension.
The window has class
.Dq nod
and type
.Sy _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_NOTIFICATION .
Compositors that blur or round windows should exclude it, e.g.\& for picom:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
blur-background-exclude = [ "class_g = 'nod'" ];
rounded-corners-exclude = [ "class_g = 'nod'" ];
.Ed
.Sh X RESOURCES
When
.Sy use_xresources
is enabled in
.Pa config.h ,
.Nm
reads the following resources at startup.
Unset resources fall back to the compiled-in defaults from
.Pa config.h .
.Bl -tag -width "nod.background.critical "
.It Sy nod.font
Fontconfig pattern for text, e.g.\& Li Noto Sans:size=11 .
.It Sy nod.monoFont
Fontconfig pattern for the header and time.
.It Sy nod.background Ns Op .urgency
Card background; falls back to
.Sy *.background .
.It Sy nod.foreground Ns Op .urgency
Text color; falls back to
.Sy *.foreground .
.It Sy nod.accent.urgency
Border, dot and button color.
Falls back to
.Sy nod.border.urgency ,
then
.Sy *.color8 ,
.Sy *.color4
and
.Sy *.color1
for low, normal and critical.
.It Sy nod.muted
Secondary text; falls back to
.Sy *.color8 .
.El
.Pp
.Ar urgency
is one of
.Sy low ,
.Sy normal ,
.Sy critical .
Because of the fallbacks, a palette generated from the wallpaper
(pywal, wallust, ...) themes
.Nm
without any nod-specific entries.
.Pp
When
.Sy use_xresources
is enabled, nod polls the X resource database every
.Sy xresources_poll_ms
milliseconds and reloads colors and font automatically.
Set
.Sy xresources_poll_ms
to 0 to disable polling; send
.Sy SIGUSR1
to force a reload.
.Pp
Example
.Pa ~/.Xresources :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nod.font:              Noto Sans:size=11
nod.monoFont:          JetBrains Mono:size=10
nod.accent.normal:     #458588
nod.accent.critical:   #cc241d
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
Start from
.Pa ~/.xinitrc
before the window manager:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
nod &
exec dwm
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nod-send 1 ,
.Xr notify-send 1 ,
.Xr gdbus 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Matteo Merola
.Sh BUGS
At most three actions are shown.
No icon, sound, or markup support by design.
Requires SDL's X11 video driver (no native Wayland).
